            "is-inline-image": false
          },
          "contents": [
            "Talk Like a Pirate Day"
          ]
        },
        ".\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "$$data_type": "org-node",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "ref": "org12bb6d2",
      "properties": {
        "post-blank": 1,
        "secondary": null,
        "mode": null,
        "granularity": null,
        "cached": null,
        "true-level": null,
        "deferred": null,
        "structure": null
      },
      "contents": [
        "People think that means yelling “ahoy” or “avast.” But that's ",
        {
          "$$data_type": "org-node",
          "type": "link",
          "ref": "org02b9c5f",
          "properties": {
            "post-blank": 1,
            "secondary": null,
            "mode": null,
            "granularity": null,
            "cached": null,
            "true-level": null,
            "deferred": null,
            "structure": null,
            "type": "id",
            "type-explicit-p": true,
            "path": "4a58286b-b997-4362-8849-68c24f65b1c9",
            "format": "bracket",
            "raw-link": "id:4a58286b-b997-4362-8849-68c24f65b1c9",
            "application": null,
            "search-option": null,
            "is-internal": false,
            "target-ref": null,
            "is-inline-image": false
          },
          "contents": [
            "Treasure Island"
          ]
        },
        "movie talk, not real pirate talk.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "$$data_type": "org-node",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "ref": "org6b1cb4d",
      "properties": {
        "post-blank": 1,
        "secondary": null,
        "mode": null,
        "granularity": null,
        "cached": null,
        "true-level": null,
        "deferred": null,
        "structure": null
      },
      "contents": [
        "Pirate talk wasn’t (just) about silly words. It was about refusing to speak the language of kings and merchants. (A very serious thing, so speaking sillily is a fine way to refuse, on its own.)\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "$$data_type": "org-node",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "ref": "orga1e8578",
      "properties": {
        "post-blank": 1,
        "secondary": null,
        "mode": null,
        "granularity": null,
        "cached": null,
        "true-level": null,
        "deferred": null,
        "structure": null
      },
      "contents": [
        "What made a pirate ship a ",
        {
          "$$data_type": "org-node",
          "type": "bold",
          "ref": "org3dfdb09",
          "properties": {
            "post-blank": 1,
            "secondary": null,
            "mode": null,
            "granularity": null,
            "cached": null,
            "true-level": null,
            "deferred": null,
            "structure": null
          },
          "contents": [
            "pirate"
          ]
        },
        "ship was that it rejected the laws of the empires around it, laws that were communicated with words. So words make a big part of that rejection ",
        {
          "$$data_type": "org-node",
          "type": "bold",
          "ref": "org3024760",
          "properties": {
            "post-blank": 0,
            "secondary": null,
            "mode": null,
            "granularity": null,
            "cached": null,
            "true-level": null,
            "deferred": null,
            "structure": null
          },
          "contents": [
            "possible"
          ]
        },
        ": pirates developed their own specific \"codes\" for how to organize their efforts, in a world dominated by one code.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "$$data_type": "org-node",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "ref": "org932208b",
      "properties": {
        "post-blank": 1,
        "secondary": null,
        "mode": null,
        "granularity": null,
        "cached": null,
        "true-level": null,
        "deferred": null,
        "structure": null
      },
      "contents": [
        "On a pirate ship, the captain wasn’t a monarch. He was elected, and he could be deposed the moment he stopped serving the crew. The quartermaster wasn’t a servant; he was the counter-power that kept the captain in check. Articles weren’t law imposed from above; they were agreements drafted and sworn collectively. If a crewmember was injured, lots of ships' code guaranteed their share, because survival depended on everyone being taken care of.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "$$data_type": "org-node",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "ref": "org4be34c8",
      "properties": {
        "post-blank": 1,
        "secondary": null,
        "mode": null,
        "granularity": null,
        "cached": null,
        "true-level": null,
        "deferred": null,
        "structure": null
      },
      "contents": [
        "That’s what gave pirate words their force. “Mate” wasn’t a gimmick. It named an equal, someone with a voice and a stake. “Share” wasn’t wages; it was recognition that the plunder belonged to all, not hoarded by bosses or thrones. Even the insults, the threats, the bravado! they came from a world where empire’s rules had no legitimacy.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "$$data_type": "org-node",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "ref": "orgcc2c4e9",
      "properties": {
        "post-blank": 1,
        "secondary": null,
        "mode": null,
        "granularity": null,
        "cached": null,
        "true-level": null,
        "deferred": null,
        "structure": null
      },
      "contents": [
        "Pirates carried the violence of their time: patriarchy, racism, brutality. They weren’t outside history. But they also proved that crews of outcasts could generate their own order, one that terrified rulers precisely because it was anarchic, egalitarian, and contagious.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "$$data_type": "org-node",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "ref": "org9d4674c",
      "properties": {
        "post-blank": 1,
        "secondary": null,
        "mode": null,
        "granularity": null,
        "cached": null,
        "true-level": null,
        "deferred": null,
        "structure": null
      },
      "contents": [
        "So if you want to talk like a pirate today, don’t (just) pretend with accents. Speak the way they did: from a code made by equals, against the legitimacy of law, in defiance of the world that tries to govern you. That’s pirate talk.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "$$data_type": "org-node",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "ref": "org2d72fe2",
      "properties": {
        "post-blank": 1,
        "secondary": null,
        "mode": null,
        "granularity": null,
        "cached": null,
        "true-level": null,
        "deferred": null,
        "structure": null
      },
      "contents": [
        "---\n"
      ]
    },
    {
